{% comment %}
  =============================================================================
  MAIN 404 ERROR PAGE SECTION
  =============================================================================
  Custom 404 error page for when users navigate to non-existent URLs
  - Centralized content layout with proper spacing
  - Localized error messages from theme locales
  - Animated content with JavaScript hooks
  - Homepage link for user navigation recovery
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  =============================================================================
  404 PAGE CONTAINER & CONTENT STRUCTURE
  =============================================================================
  Main error page container with responsive layout and animations
  - central: Centers content within page width constraints
  - content: Applies consistent content styling
  - rte: Rich text editor styling for consistent typography
  - py-medium: Vertical padding for proper spacing
  - data-cc-animate: JavaScript animation hook for page entrance
{% endcomment %}
<div class="central content rte py-medium" data-cc-animate>
  {% comment %}
    =============================================================================
    ERROR TITLE & MESSAGE
    =============================================================================
    Primary error message with localized text
    - feature-header: Consistent heading styling across theme
    - general.404.title: Localized "Page not found" message
    - general.404.subtext: Localized explanation text
    - align-center: Centers the error message for better UX
  {% endcomment %}
  <h1 class="feature-header">{{ 'general.404.title' | t }}</h1>
  <p class="align-center">{{ 'general.404.subtext' | t }} <a data-cc-animate-click href="{{ routes.root_url }}">{{ 'general.404.link' | t }}</a></p>
</div>
